{"assets":["/statement-assets/f2565eba355aef251516e7a7349bc0e643689042b98afd47ad938fd14529d0df.png","/statement-assets/2563c64b2083480cc01c8825640959df1244b74a8b03cae50b669c6b0b017954.png","/statement-assets/c29cf0b069c683c66c92418ecc4f3f1dd095b8d85e28dd9479500b84ce08d424.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1725","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Circular Mirror"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pak Chanek has a mirror in the shape of a circle. There are $$$N$$$ lamps on the circumference numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$N$$$ in clockwise order. The length of the arc from lamp $$$i$$$ to lamp $$$i+1$$$ is $$$D_i$$$ for $$$1 \\leq i \\leq N-1$$$. Meanwhile, the length of the arc between lamp $$$N$$$ and lamp $$$1$$$ is $$$D_N$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pak Chanek wants to colour the lamps with $$$M$$$ different colours. Each lamp can be coloured with one of the $$$M$$$ colours. However, there cannot be three different lamps such that the colours of the three lamps are the same and the triangle made by considering the three lamps as vertices is a right triangle (triangle with one of its angles being exactly $$$90$$$ degrees)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following are examples of lamp colouring configurations on the circular mirror."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/f2565eba355aef251516e7a7349bc0e643689042b98afd47ad938fd14529d0df.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2563c64b2083480cc01c8825640959df1244b74a8b03cae50b669c6b0b017954.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c29cf0b069c683c66c92418ecc4f3f1dd095b8d85e28dd9479500b84ce08d424.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure 1. an example of an incorrect colouring because lamps $$$1$$$, $$$2$$$, and $$$3$$$ form a right triangle"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure 2. an example of a correct colouring"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure 3. an example of a correct colouring"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Before colouring the lamps, Pak Chanek wants to know the number of distinct colouring configurations he can make. Count the number of distinct possible lamp colouring configurations, modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$N$$$ and $$$M$$$ ($$$1 \\le N \\le 3 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$2 \\le M \\le 3 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of lamps in the mirror and the number of different colours used."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$N$$$ integers $$$D_1, D_2, \\ldots, D_N$$$ ($$$1 \\le D_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the lengths of the arcs between the lamps in the mirror."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An integer representing the number of possible lamp colouring configurations, modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 2\n10 10 6 14\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 2\n10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, all correct lamp colouring configurations are $$$[1, 1, 2, 1]$$$, $$$[1, 1, 2, 2]$$$, $$$[1, 2, 1, 2]$$$, $$$[1, 2, 2, 1]$$$, $$$[1, 2, 2, 2]$$$, $$$[2, 1, 1, 1]$$$, $$$[2, 1, 1, 2]$$$, $$$[2, 1, 2, 1]$$$, $$$[2, 2, 1, 1]$$$, and $$$[2, 2, 1, 2]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1725C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1725/problem/C"}